{"id": "unknown-2026-07-31-005", "date": "2026-07-31", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New Zealand looks to legalize plug-in solar", "content": "<p>A solar regulatory review from New Zealand's Ministry for Regulation suggests legalizing plug-in solar, approving installations under 10 kW by the next working day and allowing accredited installers to sign off on an installation less than 100 kW in size without an inspection.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/31/new-zealand-looks-to-legalize-plug-in-solar/\">New Zealand looks to legalize plug-in solar</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv ma", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/31/new-zealand-looks-to-legalize-plug-in-solar/", "type": "rss"}]}
